cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "USAP — Unified Security Agent Platform"
message: "If you use USAP in research or production, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jaskarn
    family-names: Singh
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaskaranhundal/usap-skills"
url: "https://jaskaranhundal.github.io/usap-skills/"
abstract: >-
  USAP is an open-source cybersecurity skills library that turns any LLM into
  an auditable, portable security workflow runtime. It ships 79 standalone
  skills and 12 cs-* orchestrator agents across 12 security domains, a typed
  11-field JSON output contract with a hardest-line resolvable-evidence gate,
  a connector-agnostic Model Context Protocol runtime (server, router,
  dispatcher, scheduler, tamper-resistant audit chain), reproducible scoring
  (CVSS, EPSS, a written confidence rubric), and an independent held-out
  evaluation harness. Skills are framework-mapped to MITRE ATT&CK, NIST CSF
  2.0, OWASP Top 10, ATLAS, D3FEND, and the NIST AI RMF.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - llm-agents
  - model-context-protocol
  - soc-automation
  - incident-response
  - threat-hunting
  - mitre-attack
  - nist-csf
  - devsecops
  - ai-security
